Chunk 1 of 3, Phase 3 of 3 — unit ~16 of 18. Chunks 2 (inference adapter +
compact bridge) and 3 (product wiring + live certification) remain and are the
larger part of the phase; only Chunk 3's sign-off delivers the user-facing
result.

LHC-backed capture running inside Grok Build behind GROK_LHC (off by default,
host behavior bit-identical when off). Three marked core touchpoints plus the
root workspace-members entry; everything else lives in crates/lhc/grok-lhc-host.

- Capture tee on the single production ChatPersistence construction site;
  per-session worker on its own OS thread + runtime, reached by non-blocking
  try_send so the chat-state actor never blocks.
- Exhaustive ConversationItem -> MessageEventInput mapping (no wildcard arms
  over host enums, so upstream vocabulary drift is a compile error).
- Idempotency keyed on LHC's own durable thread_position.last_event_order with
  a monotonic occurrence tracker seeded from stored events — survives restart,
  replay, fork, rewind, retry, and compaction.
- 61 tests (20 unit / 37 certification / 4 golden); tripwire layer 3 now runs
  both binaries under --features test-util.

Five repair rounds, dual adversarial verification each (Sol via codex-subagent,
Opus 5 high via claude-subagent — the Fable/copilot lane was retired mid-chunk
per Lee's ruling de1c21f after rate-limit saturation; no Fable verdict was used).

Orchestrator amendments, recorded per the escalation rule:

- A1: replaced a non-atomic {thread}.meta.json sidecar with LHC's in-database
  last_event_order. The sidecar could desync from the SQLite whose keys it
  controlled, silently reinstating the swallow defect it fixed.
- B1: superseded my OWN round-2 ruling ("emit nothing on replace_history") on
  factual grounds. Its premise was false: replace_history has five production
  callers in xai-chat-state, three of which are ADDITIVE — dangling-tool repair
  (mutations.rs:68), memory-reminder injection during request build
  (request_builder.rs:59), and the CompactionMeta summary (mutations.rs:445).
  Emit-nothing dropped all three. Now: submit without bumping generation and
  let LHC's own dedup act as the diff.
- C1: an unrequested implementor change put blocking_recv on the production
  path, panicking at every session spawn with the feature on. All 53 tests
  passed anyway, because every one called the adapter from a synchronous
  #[test]. Caught by an orchestrator probe reproducing the host's async call
  shape; permanent async-convention guards added.

Two verifier findings accepted rather than fixed, documented in FORK.md
"Accepted limitations": the hook-2/hook-3 session-id coupling is verifiable
only by inspection (a test would need a fourth core touchpoint), and the
async guards catch panicking blocks but hang rather than fail fast on silent
ones. Trivial residue fixed by the orchestrator: three
#[allow(clippy::await_holding_lock)] with justification, verified truthful by
Sol.

patches/ regeneration follows in the next commit.

